abstract: >-
  TrustCal studies whether evidence-grounded trust reduces sycophantic collapse
  in multi-agent scientific debate relative to a matched majority-vote control,
  and where verifier accuracy and evidence redundancy place its boundary. The
  repository contains the Python pipeline, the pre-registered evaluation plan,
  the controlled-benchmark design, the full project report, and the journal
  manuscript. P0 engineering is released; the confirmatory Core and Full
  matrices have not been run, so no efficacy result is claimed.
